# XSH wcscat()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Sources are in arrays and destinations are filled with L'X' first, so that codes written past the terminator show.

assertion  XSH.wcscat.001
anchor     functions/wcscat.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wcscat.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       wcscat() appends the source string, null code included, to the
           end of the destination string: "ab" and "cd" give "abcd" with a
           null at index 4, nothing after it is changed, and the call
           returns the destination pointer.
test       t/001-append.c

assertion  XSH.wcscat.002
anchor     functions/wcscat.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       wcscat() of "xyz" onto an empty destination gives "xyz"; of an
           empty string onto "ab" leaves "ab", with the null at index 2 and
           nothing after it changed.
test       t/002-empty.c

assertion  XSH.wcscat.003
anchor     functions/wcscat.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       wcscat() leaves errno unchanged on valid input, both when it is 0
           and when it is EDOM.
test       t/003-errno-kept.c
